    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 29-layer SiO2/Al2O3 multilayer coating on fused silica substrate for solar-blind UV bandpass filtering. Layer sequence: alternating SiO2/Al2O3 starting with SiO2 (layer 1), total 29 finite layers. Initialize layers 1-10 as quarter-wave at 267.5 nm (SiO2 ~39 nm, Al2O3 ~67.5 nm), layers 11-13 as asymmetric cavity (66.0 nm SiO2, 67.5 nm Al2O3, 69.0 nm SiO2), layers 14-29 as alternating Al2O3/SiO2 quarter-wave. Optimization bounds: ±20% around initialization. Objective: maximize mean transmittance in 255-280 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with coherent TMM solver. Air incidence, unpolarized or average of s/p. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
